# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SANNIDH  ·  Production Environment Variables
#  File: .env.production
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  HOW TO USE
#  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  1. Copy this file: cp .env.production.example .env.production
#  2. Fill in your credentials below (never commit .env.production to git)
#  3. Run: npm run build
#
#  In SANDBOX mode (VITE_ENV=sandbox), the app runs 100% without any API keys.
#  All gateways return realistic mock data so you can test the full UI flow.
#  Switch to VITE_ENV=production only when you have live credentials.
#
#  ⚠ SECURITY: Never commit this file to Git. It is listed in .gitignore.
#    All values here are read at BUILD TIME (VITE_ prefix = public bundle).
#    Secrets that must stay server-side go in Supabase Edge Function env vars.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── ENVIRONMENT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 'production' to enable live API calls.
# Set to 'sandbox'    to run with realistic mock data (no API keys needed).
VITE_ENV=sandbox


# ─── SUPABASE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_ID.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Supabase Service Role Key — NEVER expose this in client code.
# Used only in Supabase Edge Functions (server-side).
# Store via: supabase secrets set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=xxx
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key_here


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  HEART API #1 — GSTN / GSP Gateway
#  (GST Suvidha Provider for live GSTN API access)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  How to get these keys:
#  1. Register as a GSP or use a licensed GSP partner:
#     → ClearTax API: https://developer.cleartax.in
#     → Iris Peridot:  https://iris.in/gsp
#     → Cygnet:        https://cygnetgsp.in
#     → NIC Sandbox:   https://sandbox.gstin.gov.in (for testing only)
#  2. After registration, you receive:
#     → Client ID (app_key)
#     → Client Secret (secret)
#     → GSTN Username (your company's GST login username)
#  3. Paste them below.
#
#  Cost: ₹0 for NIC Sandbox (testing) · ₹5,000–₹15,000/month for production GSP
#
VITE_GSP_BASE_URL=https://commonapi.gst.gov.in
VITE_GSP_CLIENT_ID=your_gsp_client_id_here
VITE_GSP_CLIENT_SECRET=your_gsp_client_secret_here
VITE_GSP_USERNAME=your_gstn_portal_username_here


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  HEART API #2 — RBI Account Aggregator (Bank Feed)
#  (Real-time bank transactions via RBI's AA framework)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  How to get these keys:
#  1. Register as a Financial Information User (FIU) with an AA provider:
#     → Setu AA:     https://setu.co/products/account-aggregator
#     → FinVu:       https://finvu.in (most popular, 100+ banks)
#     → Anumati:     https://anumati.in
#     → PhonePe AA:  https://developer.phonepe.com/aa
#  2. After FIU registration (takes 1–2 weeks + RBI documentation):
#     → You receive an API Key
#     → A unique Entity ID (your FIU handle)
#     → Sandbox and Production base URLs
#  3. Paste them below.
#
#  Cost: Free sandbox · ₹2–₹5 per consent per year in production
#  Banks supported: HDFC, ICICI, SBI, Axis, Kotak, Yes Bank, PNB, BOB, + 90 more
#
VITE_AA_API_BASE_URL=https://api.finvu.in/v2
VITE_AA_API_KEY=your_aa_api_key_here
VITE_AA_ENTITY_ID=your_fiu_entity_id_here


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  HEART API #3 — OCR Document Processing
#  (Extract invoice data from PDF/image uploads)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Choose ONE provider: 'google' (recommended) or 'aws'
#
#  OPTION A — Google Cloud Vision API (recommended for India invoices)
#  How to get key:
#  1. Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com
#  2. Create a project → Enable "Cloud Vision API"
#  3. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create API Key
#  4. Restrict key to "Cloud Vision API" only
#  Cost: First 1,000 units/month FREE · $1.50 per 1,000 after that
#
VITE_OCR_PROVIDER=google
VITE_GOOGLE_VISION_API_KEY=your_google_cloud_vision_api_key_here

#  OPTION B — AWS Textract (alternative, better for tables/forms)
#  How to get key:
#  1. Go to: https://aws.amazon.com/textract
#  2. IAM → Create User → Attach "AmazonTextractFullAccess" policy
#  3. Generate Access Key ID + Secret
#  Cost: First 1,000 pages/month FREE · $0.015 per page after that
#
# VITE_OCR_PROVIDER=aws
# VITE_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aws_access_key_id
# VITE_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_aws_secret_access_key
# VITE_AWS_REGION=ap-south-1


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  OPTIONAL — Email Invoice Inbox (for automatic email-to-ledger parsing)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Set up a dedicated email address like: invoices@yourdomain.com
#  Then configure your email provider (SendGrid / Postmark / Mailgun) to
#  forward inbound emails to your Supabase Edge Function webhook.
#
#  How to configure inbound email webhook:
#  → SendGrid Inbound Parse: https://docs.sendgrid.com/for-developers/parsing-email/setting-up-the-inbound-parse-webhook
#  → Postmark Inbound:       https://postmarkapp.com/developer/user-guide/inbound
#
#  These are stored in Supabase Edge Function secrets, not here.
#  supabase secrets set SENDGRID_API_KEY=xxx
#  supabase secrets set INBOUND_EMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=xxx


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Before going live, complete these steps in order:
#
#  [ ] 1. Set VITE_ENV=production in this file
#  [ ] 2. Fill in all 3 Heart API credentials above
#  [ ] 3. Run the production RLS SQL migration:
#         supabase db push  (or paste migration in Supabase SQL Editor)
#  [ ] 4. Deploy Supabase Edge Functions (bank webhook, email parser):
#         supabase functions deploy fiu-bank-feed
#         supabase functions deploy email-invoice-parser
#  [ ] 5. Build the production bundle:
#         npm run build
#  [ ] 6. Deploy to Vercel / Netlify / your hosting:
#         vercel --prod   OR   netlify deploy --prod
#  [ ] 7. Test with a real bank CSV upload → verify it appears in ledger
#  [ ] 8. Test with a real GSTR-2B JSON → verify ITC blocked/eligible updates
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
